WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.168
-We don't always have
enough time

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.169
to cover all of the recent news,

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.169
so here with a recap

00:00:04.169 --> 00:00:05.171
is one of our writers,

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:06.472
Amber Ruffin, in a segment

00:00:06.472 --> 00:00:08.040
we call "Amber Says What."

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.743
♪♪

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:11.811
-You guys!

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.412
Things. have. been. crazy.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:14.580
Okay, so, recently,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.983
the state of Texas
had a winter emergency

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.484
and I was like, "What?!

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:21.254
Texas had a winter emergency?

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:23.522
Oh, Lord, we done
broke the Earth!"

00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:26.459
Then, I found out that this
caused millions of Texans

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.894
to go without heat or water
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:31.731
Then, I found out that it was
at this exact moment

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:35.001
that Texas Senator Ted Cruz
chose to go to Cancún

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.302
and I was like, "What?!

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:38.371
Then, he blamed his children
for the trip

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.839
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.775
Then, I found out
he left his dog at home

00:00:42.775 --> 00:00:44.410
and I was like, "What?!"

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.712
[ Laughter ]
How could you leave
a dog at home

00:00:46.712 --> 00:00:49.281
when you, sir, also are a dog?

00:00:49.281 --> 00:00:51.717
Now, I know everyone rags
on you a ton, Ted,

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:53.553
but maybe it's not enough?

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.921
Look at that dog!

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.389
Poor thing!

00:00:56.389 --> 00:01:00.526
How bad do you have
to have it to miss Ted Cruz?

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:01.627
[ Laughter ]
Dang!

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:04.163
Then, something
really cute happened!

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:07.433
Okay, so this extra fluffy sheep
was found in the wild

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:10.936
and they ended up shaving
78 pounds of wool from it.

00:01:10.936 --> 00:01:12.405
And I was like, "What?!"

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.140
Well, it's a good thing
you got a haircut,

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.809
because your hair
was getting too long!

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:19.245
Hey, Seth, did you hear
what I said to the sheep?

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.847
-Yeah.
-I said that its hair

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.948
was too long.
-Yeah.

00:01:22.948 --> 00:01:25.718
-I suggested
that it get a haircut.

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:26.852
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, I heard what you said.

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:28.121
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.989
[ Laughter ]
Anyway, Naomi Osaka was

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.558
at the Australian Open
when this happened --

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:33.960 line:0%
-Playing around her.
Yeah, there it is.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.895 line:0%
-Aww!
-A fan yells out,

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:37.563 line:0%
"There's a butterfly
on your legs,"

00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:38.764 line:0%
and, now, Osaka's going

00:01:38.764 --> 00:01:41.234 line:0%
to take it to safety.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.002
-I saw that and I was like,
"What?!"

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.137
Isn't that cute?

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.272
That butterfly is all of us.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.640
We all think Naomi's perfect,

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.775
and want to give her
a little kiss on the nose!

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:51.811
And then, when the butterfly
wouldn't leave,

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:55.915
Naomi gently took it
off of her face and set it down!

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.383
I saw that and was like,
"What?!"

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.584
She is so sweet!

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:01.053
Because, if a butterfly
landed on my face

00:02:01.053 --> 00:02:02.622
in the middle of a really
important thing,

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.090
I'd have just smashed it
because [bleep] a butterfly.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:08.093
[ Laughter ]
Then, the funniest thing
in the world happened!

00:02:08.093 --> 00:02:10.997
A Texas attorney,
during a trial,

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.365
could not get rid
of his Zoom filter. Look.

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:15.401
-Can you hear me, Judge?

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.903 line:0%
-I can hear you.
I think it's a filter.

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:21.073 line:0%
-It is. I don't know how
to remove it.

00:02:21.073 --> 00:02:25.344 line:0%
I've got my assistant here.
She's trying to, but --

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:28.547 line:0%
I'm prepared
to go forward with it.

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.049
I'm here live.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.617
I'm not a cat.

00:02:31.617 --> 00:02:33.619
-I saw that and was like,
"What

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:35.788
are you, if you aren't a cat?

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.790
You sure look
like a cat to me."

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.791
"I am not a cat."

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.260
That's exactly what a cat

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.295
would say, you cat-ass cat.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.430
[ Laughter ]
Then, I heard a harrowing tale

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.499
of ingenuity and perseverance.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.901
The tale of the
Gorilla Glue Girl.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:52.272
So, okay, this lady had used
Gorilla Glue to do her hair

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:54.173
and she couldn't get it out!

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:55.240
And then, she was like, "What?!"

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.509
And I was like, "What

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.976
did you think
was going to happen?"

00:02:57.976 --> 00:03:00.013
It's glue.
All it does is glue.

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:02.014
So she went online
and told her story

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:04.650
and everyone was offering
suggestions about what to do.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.486
And I was like,
"What could she possibly do?!"

00:03:07.486 --> 00:03:08.554
It's glue.

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:10.123
Glue. gonna. glue.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:12.992
And then, I, like every other
person who heard this story,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:17.263
became obsessed with her and I
needed her to be okay, so badly!

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.097
She was so sad in the video!

00:03:19.097 --> 00:03:20.866
And it's not. her. fault!

00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:22.768
We all did crazy things
when we were young!

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:23.770
It's fine!

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.105
Then, I found out she's 40!

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.341
And I was like,
[ Laughing ] "What?"

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.609
[ Laughter ]
Oh, no!

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:32.110
Then, a doctor reached out
to her and said,

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:35.014
"I can remove it for free,"
and I was like, "What?"

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:37.483
But then, he did,
and her hair looked perfect

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:38.851
and I was like, "What?!"

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:42.188
And then, a whole nation
rejoiced, like, "What?! What?!"

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:45.925
Then, I found out that these two
are going to have a second baby

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:46.925
and I was like, "What?!"

00:03:46.925 --> 00:03:48.160
Yay! I love it!

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.428
But I looked online

00:03:49.428 --> 00:03:52.631
and these British people
were so mad at her.

00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:54.300
I mean, they've always
been mad at her,

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:55.667
but this time I was like,
"What

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:59.304
are you so mad about,
that this woman is pregnant?"

00:03:59.304 --> 00:04:01.040
You're going to be mad
that a man and his wife

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.709
are having their second child?

00:04:02.709 --> 00:04:05.677
I wonder what it is
about her you don't like.

00:04:05.677 --> 00:04:07.313
What could it possibly be

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.415
that has those British people
so on edge?

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:12.451
What about her contribution
to the royal bloodline

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:14.153
has them angry?

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.688
Well, we may never know.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:18.624
[ Laughter ]
Then the Britney Spears
documentary came out

00:04:18.624 --> 00:04:20.559
and people were all like,
"Free Britney!"

00:04:20.559 --> 00:04:23.096
Crying and stuff in the little
"Free Britney" T-shirts.

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:24.663
And I was all like, "What?!"

00:04:24.663 --> 00:04:28.367
Then, I watched the movie
and I was like, "What?

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:29.668
Get me a T-shirt!"

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:31.104
So, okay, here's what happens.

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:34.072
Like her dad had control
of her money and stuff

00:04:34.072 --> 00:04:37.009
and she refused to perform
until that stopped.

00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:38.110
And I was like, "What?!"

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.444
Then, it happened.

00:04:39.444 --> 00:04:41.714
They went to court and her dad
lost financial control

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:44.183
in her conservatorship
and I was like, "What?!"

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.085
Even though I still
don't fully understand

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.453
what a conservatorship is.

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.622
Like this girl is almost 40

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:51.724
and controls nothing
of her life.

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.693
If anyone needs
a conservatorship,

00:04:53.693 --> 00:04:55.061
it's Gorilla Glue Lady.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:56.562
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:58.797
Then everyone was like,
"Did you see

00:04:58.797 --> 00:05:01.534
the new United States
Postal Service mail truck?"

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:02.768
And I was like, "What?!

00:05:02.768 --> 00:05:04.236
No. Why would I?"

00:05:04.236 --> 00:05:06.038
And then, there were like,
"You got to see it."

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:07.239
And I was like, "What?!"

00:05:07.239 --> 00:05:09.308
But then I saw it.
I was like,

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:10.877
"What?!

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:12.678
What happened?!"

00:05:12.678 --> 00:05:16.315
Did this truck drive through
the space-time continuum?

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:17.450
What is this?

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.018
What are you delivering,
the Pope?

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:21.921
Who designed this truck,
Homer Simpson?!

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:23.489
What even is this?!

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.224
You know what I think
this truck is?

00:05:25.224 --> 00:05:26.225
I -- Oh.

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:27.226
Whoa, wait.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:28.861
[ Laughter ]
How beautiful!

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.596
A butterfly!

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.498
I'm going to get it!
[ Clap ]

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.566
[ Laughter ]
I got business to do!

00:05:34.566 --> 00:05:36.969
I killed it!
This has been "Amber Says What."

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.738
♪♪

